--- SURFACE SUMMARY (parity with the web source) -----------------------------------
DrivingTab is the analytics Driving tab. The web component is PRESENTATIONAL: it takes
`data: FleetAnalytics | undefined` as a prop and binds only useTranslation + useUnits (no
fetch). The native port mirrors that exactly (the XRayBucketChart presentational precedent):
the WinUI-free DrivingTabProjection turns a DrivingTabModel (parent-owned load phase +
drive_analytics payload) + UnitPref + ILocalizer into a render-ready DrivingTabDisplay; the
DrivingTab ContentControl is a thin renderer. The view performs no HTTP.

States (every state renders — no hidden surfaces):
  Loading  -> skeleton chrome (reduce-motion aware)
  Error    -> TsQueryError + retry (raises RetryRequested; the parent owns the refetch)
  Stale    -> section scaffold + a "Stale" TsStatusPill (mqtt.stale)
  Offline  -> section scaffold + an "Offline" TsStatusPill (common.offline)
  Empty    -> the full section scaffold with every section showing its own empty state
              (web parity for data === undefined)
  Ready    -> the populated section scaffold

Sections reproduced (all of them):
  1. DrivingPerformanceCards  : 6 TsMetricCard (Top/Avg Speed km/h->display, Peak Power/Regen kW,
                                Avg/Longest Drive km->display); each card em-dashes when its stat is absent.
  2. Speed Distribution       : bar (range/count) | "No speed data"
  3. Trip Distance Distribution: bar             | "No distance distribution data"
  4. Hourly Driving Pattern   : composed bar(drives)+line(distance, raw km per web) | "No hourly data"
  5. Temperature vs Efficiency: scatter (temp C->display, eff Wh/km->Wh/mi when miles, dist converted) | "No temperature data"
  6. Daily Driving Trend      : composed area(distance, raw km)+line(drives) | "No daily trend data"
  7. Drive Duration Distribution: bar           | "Not enough drive data for distribution chart"
  8. Efficiency Trend         : area over daily_trend filtered efficiency>0 | "No efficiency trend data"
  9. DrivingTemperatureStats  : 6 TsMetricCard (inside/outside min/avg/max C->display) | "No temperature stats"

Boundary unit conversion (display boundary only, SI/derived-SI in): UnitConverters.SpeedFromSi/
DistanceFromSi/TemperatureFromSi via useUnits()-equivalent UnitPref. Charts use the shared
native chart library (TsComposedChart, each series rendered by its ChartSeriesKind) — never a
direct charting-lib import. i18n: every string flows through the ILocalizer facade; all 33
analytics.driving.* keys + the reused chrome keys (analytics.tabs.driving, error.loadFailed,
error.retry, common.loading/offline, mqtt.stale) exist in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw
(no new keys required). Accessibility: AutomationProperties.SetName on the root, every panel,
chart, metric card and chip; reduce-motion honoured by the skeletons + TsFadeIn. Diagnostics:
DrivingTabDiagnostics.RecordViewOpened() emits "view.opened slug=DrivingTab" (PII-safe — never a
drive metric).

Tests (DrivingTabTests.cs, 37 headless cases): state projection (loading/empty/error/stale/
offline/ready), the seven sections' data+empty branches and series shapes (kinds, palette
indices, range/date/hour labels, efficiency>0 filter), the performance + temperature grids'
unit conversions (metric vs imperial, em-dash gating), the temp-vs-efficiency boundary
conversion (10C->50F, 150 Wh/km->241.4016 Wh/mi), a11y names on every state/section/card, and
the diagnostics (slug + PII-safety).

